{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals","id":983381,"title":"Abyssal Supernals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T09:58:56-07:00","id":983381,"title":"Abyssal Supernals?","content":"So, &quot;Abyssal&quot; is kind of a psuedo-template applied to Spirits (for Gulmoth) or Goetia (for Acamoth). Not really a template, so much as &quot;model them using these rules&quot;. (Ghost rules probably don't work because of Integrity, Anchors, and maybe Virtue and Vice.)<br /> <br /> What about Supernal Entities? They are mostly modeled with Ephemeral Entity rules too, excepting they have Arcana instead of Influences and don't have Twilight Form as a default Manifestation. What would an &quot;Abyssal&quot; Entity be like, using their Influence/Arcana in a corrupted fashion (like Scelesti)? The &quot;Corpus degrades in the Fallen World&quot; could be retained to represent how they too can't stay here long before the Abyss reclaims them.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Regarding the concept in general, use in games, or specific &quot;mirrored&quot; Supernal-&gt;Abyssal Entities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:01:19-07:00","id":983384,"title":"","content":"It's possible since the Abyss collects Supernal beings that &quot;die&quot; when in the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:06:15-07:00","id":983388,"title":"","content":"It might just be an ephemeral entity thing. But since it's the Abyss nothing is impossible. Abyssal Firestorms and Pandorans, strix and huntsmen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:32:13-07:00","id":984485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=983388#post983388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be an ephemeral entity thing. But since it's the Abyss nothing is impossible. Abyssal Firestorms and Pandorans, strix and huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal, Inferno-touched Machine Angels and Spirits Hive-Claiming a Sin-Eater that's under Strix control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:14:06-07:00","id":984508,"title":"","content":"Abyssal Supernals? That's a paradox! <br /> <br /> (sorry for the pun.....)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(not sorry)</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:21:42-07:00","id":984595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=984508#post984508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal Supernals? That's a paradox!<br /> <br /> (sorry for the pun.....)<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(not sorry)</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Booooo!</li> <li>I kind of think the distinction between &quot;Abyssal&quot; and &quot;Supernal&quot; is baloney. I mean, the only meaningful difference between Abyss and Supernal is that one is reflected in the Fallen and one isn't, and considering the Fallen World is, by definition, false, it's not a great thing to define things by.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:38:29-07:00","id":984602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=984595#post984595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the only meaningful difference between Abyss and Supernal is that one is reflected in the Fallen and one isn't, and considering the Fallen World is, by definition, false, it's not a great thing to define things by.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand what you mean, for everyone it matters to, it's the difference between fiction and non-fiction, real and unreal, natural and unnatural.<br /> <br /> I take the Neolithic view, where the Abyss is not a fully antagonistic force. It's there, past the 'edges' of reality where it belongs. The problem is that the Fall has caused some rips in the world where it shouldn't be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2016, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:07:42-07:00","id":984609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=984595#post984595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of think the distinction between &quot;Abyssal&quot; and &quot;Supernal&quot; is baloney. I mean, the only meaningful difference between Abyss and Supernal is that one is reflected in the Fallen and one isn't,</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is coherence. That's the entire point of the Scelesti ideology. Also, the Abyss is very much reflected in the Fallen World, that's a basic problem of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and considering the Fallen World is, by definition, false, it's not a great thing to define things by. </div> </div> </div>Fallen means it's damaged not that it's not real. It's very real and the Supernal needs the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T22:16:02-07:00","id":984750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=984508#post984508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>(not sorry)</i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As well you should<span style=\"font-size:8px\">n't</span> be!<br /> <br /> While I agree with Michael on the point about the Fallen being abyssal <i>and</i> supernal, I wouldn't infer that the Fallen World is <i>needed by</i> the supernal simply because the interaction is two-way. That's not actually a logical requirement of their relationship.<br /> <br /> (This is not to say it's unreasonable, because it certainly is <b>not</b>. It fits fine and is a workable interpretation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:28:35-07:00","id":984915,"title":"","content":"I am a fan of the Abyss-as-Qlippoth interpretation; that the Abyss is an inevitable by-product of an imperfectly perceived cosmos. It is the product of false dualism; given reality by ignorance gifting force to the probability. From that, it contains near-infinite possibility but no actual truth.<br /> <br /> You could phrase it that the Abyss is a subjective reality creeping into a universe built of objective truth; polluting and perverting reality with possibilities it was never meant to have. And it is so hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:26:40-07:00","id":985067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=984915#post984915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a fan of the Abyss-as-Qlippoth interpretation; that the Abyss is an inevitable by-product of an imperfectly perceived cosmos. It is the product of false dualism; given reality by ignorance gifting force to the probability. From that, it contains near-infinite possibility but no actual truth.<br /> <br /> You could phrase it that the Abyss is a subjective reality creeping into a universe built of objective truth; polluting and perverting reality with possibilities it was never meant to have. And it is so hungry.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if, jumping off that, the ChroD Abyss contains the subjective, consensus-based Old World of Darkness? And the Technocrats' agenda of forcing everyone into a consensus threatens to &quot;lock in&quot; reality and force it free from the Abyss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:33:53-07:00","id":985073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983381-abyssal-supernals?p=985067#post985067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if, jumping off that, the ChroD Abyss contains the subjective, consensus-based Old World of Darkness? And the Technocrats' agenda of forcing everyone into a consensus threatens to &quot;lock in&quot; reality and force it free from the Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also have every Dungeons and Dragons setting and every thing that isn't real. Infinity is pretty big. We just know of more notable ones, like the Prince of Leaves' alternate history, who have been drawn to the Fallen world.<br /> <br /> But presumably that's how the Fallen World came into play in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:14:29-07:00","id":985139,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about this as an example being?<br /> <br /> Phantoms: Abyssal entities of Death<br /> Represent death as the Final End, the Ultimate Entropy (rather than a state of transition). They whisper (in the sepulchral rattle of dying breaths) of the pointlessness of existence, and how all of a Mage's efforts will end in nothing. Uses their Death Arcanum to create mockeries of unlife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:18:48-07:00","id":985141,"title":"","content":"That seems more like an Exarch's minion. Or an Inferno creature, or a spirit one.<br /> <br /> The Abyss isn't evil, or even necessarily negative, though it can be. It's just weird and spreads pervasively like an infection.<br /> <br /> You should check out <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/25526/Intruders-Encounters-With-the-Abyss\" target=\"_blank\">Intruders</a>, it's full of Abyssal intrusions. There's the Abyssal Assistant, which appears to people struggling and stressed in their attempts to invent something. It gives them ideas, and allows them to build far out concepts that are within the realm of possibility but certainly push it to its limits. The inventor finds themselves addicted to it, slowly turning pieces of the world into impossible constructs. And they work. If a scientist took a look at it it wouldn't make sense, and only the inventor can fix them, but they work. In the meantime it drains energy from the surrounding area and the inventor becomes increasingly addicted to his creating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T13:40:30-07:00","id":986927,"title":"","content":"I've always liked to think of the Abyss as the place where all symbols that aren't in the Supernal are and when new symbols appear or disappear in the Supernal they're usually just being shuffled between the two. Mages who Ascend are probably an exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}